    roots_desc: "<b>How it works on fingers:</b> If you plug in x = r₁ <i>('ex equals ar-one')</i>, the first bracket becomes zero (r₁ − r₁ = 0) and multiplies the entire expression to zero! So r₁, r₂, r₃ are the exact pins pinning the curve to the X-axis. Drag sliders r₁, r₂, r₃ (or drag the roots on the graph) and watch the expanded coefficients update live!",
