    sl_bezier_t: "Parameter t (0 to 1)",
    bezier_explain: "<b>Bézier Curve — B(t) = Σ Pₖ·bₖ(t)</b> <i>(spoken: 'bee of tee equals the sum of control points pee-kay times Bernstein polynomials bee-kay of tee')</i>. Points P₁ and P₂ act like smooth magnets pulling a silk thread without forcing it to pierce through them. Drag P₀..P₃ with your mouse directly on the canvas! Every TrueType/OpenType font, SVG icon, and car body panel is built this way.",
    lagrange_explain: "<b>Lagrange Interpolation — L(x) = Σ yₖ·lₖ(x)</b> <i>(spoken: 'el of ex equals the sum of heights why-kay times Lagrange basis polynomials el-kay')</i>. This polynomial is forced to pierce all 4 points strictly. Drag any point with your mouse: near the boundaries the curve whips into violent loops! That is <b>Runge's phenomenon</b> — the exact reason 3D CAD and graphics use Bézier splines instead of one giant polynomial.",

