    w2_story:
      "<b>What this is & how to read h = |P(x + iy)|:</b> Writing <b>x + iy</b> <i>(spoken: 'ex plus eye times why', where <b>i = √−1</b> is the imaginary unit meaning 'step 90° sideways')</i> widens the narrow X-line into a square glass floor. Above every point of that floor we plot height <b>|P(x + iy)|</b> <i>('modulus of pee of zee', the distance from zero, so height is always ≥ 0 like a stretched rubber trampoline)</i>. The <b>bright yellow neon seam down the middle (at y = 0)</b> is literally your 2D school graph from Window #1! And the <b>sharp funnels poking the glass floor at height 0</b> are the roots. Lift the parabola with <b>a₀</b>: the central seam lifts into the air, while the two root funnels simply walk sideways onto the glass floor!",
