      "<b>Where 4D comes from & how to read z₁ⁿ + z₂ⁿ = c:</b> Each complex variable has two real coordinates: <b>z₁ = x₁ + i·y₁</b> <i>('zee-one equals ex-one plus eye why-one')</i> and <b>z₂ = x₂ + i·y₂</b> <i>('zee-two equals ex-two plus eye why-two')</i>. Together they span <b>2 + 2 = 4 spatial dimensions (x₁, y₁, x₂, y₂)</b>! Wrapping the infinite 3D trampoline from Window #2 into a 4D hypersphere <b>S³</b> <i>(spoken: 'es-three' — the 3D surface of a 4D ball)</i> and projecting it to 3D reveals these nested glowing tori. At degree <b>n = 5</b> you get the famous <b>Calabi–Yau quintic manifold</b> — the microscopic origami into which string theory curls the extra dimensions of our Universe!",
